{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473560-achieving-unboundable-merit","id":1473560,"title":"Achieving Unboundable merit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-01-30T02:11:47-08:00","id":1473560,"title":"Achieving Unboundable merit","content":"&quot;Unboundable&quot; is a mysterious merit who has no specific explanation and according to the core books, it's feared, hated and sometimes object of research from vampires.<br /> <br /> Here's a the question.<br /> In RAW it's possible to weaken or ignore the Blood Bound through expenditure of Willpower, but only for a brief time ranging from a scene to a single turn ( and it still requires a difficulty 8 Willpower roll ).<br /> Yet a mortal who sleeps well can reasonably expend up to 300-350 Willpower points in a year.<br /> <br /> In your opinion, in RAI, could a ghoul slowly build the Unboundable merit by spending<b><i> thousands</i></b> of Willpower points through several years?<br /> <br /> ( I already tackle the obvious objection &quot;unruly ghouls are killed&quot;: the Blood Bond requires spending Willpower even only for plotting against the domitor, so trying to build an immunity definetly count as plotting, and can be done in secret: a silent struggle of Willpower against the Bond, all in the ghoul's mind )<br /> ( I tackle another objection &quot;if that was possible, all Methuselah would do that&quot;, ghouls have something vampires has not: a living soul. It's what allows some humans to perform Sorcery or High Magic )<br /> <br /> Ancillary questions:<br /> <br /> 1- Can some Merits help ( I found those: Iron Will, Coldly Logical, ) ?<br /> 2- Can some Flaws also help ( I found those: Self-Preservation, Problem with Authority ) ?<br /> 3- Can some Skills - specializations help ( introspective meditation / Academics - theology , self-hypnosis / Science - psychotherapy , self-examination / Medicine - psychoanalysis ) ?<br /> 4- Nature can't be changed at will, but adherence to an appropriate Demeanor emphatizing rebellion ( Anarchist, Deviant, Rebel ) or self-affermation ( Autocrat, Loner, Rogue ) for many years can help?<br /> 5- Hedge Magic, mortal alchemy and other application of the Occult skill may help?<br /> 6- True Faith in something evil ( the Infernal Faith described in Devil's due ) or Resolve ( again, Devil's Due ) may help?<br /> <br /> Finally, I have found a Merit who, in my opinion, may support the notion that is possible to become resistant to the Blood Bound through pratice ( Guide to the Camarilla, page 76 )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Broken Bond (4pt. Merit)</b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">You were once blood-bound but have secretly slipped the leash, and you are free to act as you will once more. Your regnant has no idea that you are not in fact bound, and continues to treat you as if you were. <i>At Storyteller discretion, the experience of having been bound once may render you immune to ever being enthralled again.</i></span></span></span></b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27051,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","user":"Solomon Draak","date":". 01-30-2022, 05:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T05:11:27-08:00","id":1473566,"title":"","content":"Just as the Blood Bond is magic, immunity to the Blood Bond is also magical. People with very low willpower can get it. People with the Follower nature can get it. There's no sort of requirement or anything for getting it. So I'd personally steer clear of any hard rules about what people can do to gain the merit. Instead I'd just keep it as some sort of mystical thing, and people who end up with the merit tend to justify it however they want or can, and the same with those researching them tend to find justifications (they'd point towards the person's nature or social merits or high willpower or whatever).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T06:45:17-08:00","id":1473570,"title":"","content":"I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a>. The Unbondable merit is mystical in nature and does not require any specific prerequisites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T12:05:43-08:00","id":1473591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473560-achieving-unboundable-merit?p=1473566#post1473566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just as the Blood Bond is magic, immunity to the Blood Bond is also magical. People with very low willpower can get it. People with the Follower nature can get it. There's no sort of requirement or anything for getting it. So I'd personally steer clear of any hard rules about what people can do to gain the merit. Instead I'd just keep it as some sort of mystical thing, and people who end up with the merit tend to justify it however they want or can, and the same with those researching them tend to find justifications (they'd point towards the person's nature or social merits or high willpower or whatever).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, let me reformulate.<br /> Should something similar to that merit be achievable through training and effort, RAI?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T07:52:23-08:00","id":1473752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473560-achieving-unboundable-merit?p=1473591#post1473591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should something similar to that merit be achievable through training and effort, RAI?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. <br /> <br /> There are no rules (V20, afaik) around gaining merits after a character has been created, thus the only conclusion we can draw as to the _intention_ of the rules is that it cannot be achieved by training and effort. If a house rule (or some obscure rule I don't know about) allows you to expend XP for Merits then yes, it can be gained, and it's up to the ST &amp; player to justify it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T02:17:52-08:00","id":1473891,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11490_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11490\" data-vbnamecard=\"11490\">Dogstar</a><br /> <br /> Merits can not be gained after 'creation', but often their effects can.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27051_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27051\" data-vbnamecard=\"27051\">Solomon Draak</a><br /> <br /> If you want to achieve the effect, participating in a vaulderie could accomplish this but that is not what you asked.<br /> <br /> Raw you can't break a bond by training or willpower alone and I'm fairly sure that's intentional.<br /> <br /> If it were possible, there would be no Sabbat, no Jyhad. The vampiric society would be vastly different.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26274,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26274-moriaki","user":"Moriaki","date":". 02-03-2022, 08:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26274-moriaki","name":"Moriaki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26274_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T03:27:40-08:00","id":1473959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moriaki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473560-achieving-unboundable-merit?p=1473891#post1473891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11490_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11490\" data-vbnamecard=\"11490\">Dogstar</a><br /> <br /> Merits can not be gained after 'creation', but often their effects can.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, and where I've seen it happen it's usually by ST fiat, a house rule allowing their purchase, or a reward from a campaign storyline.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}